## Summary

Reframe Home around current connection/safety/access/project state while preserving the existing granular permission switches and main-process authority model.

## Changes

- add a four-metric Home cockpit for connection, safety/read-only posture, published tool surface + effective permission count, and approved project aliases;
- add one calm attention row that routes setup blockers, activity problems, or connection errors to the existing Setup / Activity / Diagnostics surfaces;
- make Permissions the primary Home surface and stack Folders + Health as supporting state at wide widths;
- preserve the existing 900 / 720 / 520px effective-width strategy so resize and 125/150/200% zoom compress the same way;
- distinguish effective permission settings from published/cached tool schemas with explicit copy that live enforcement changes immediately while ChatGPT may retain an older schema until a new conversation;
- allow several permission disclosures to stay expanded independently without changing any adjacent checkbox or settings IPC path;
- add focused JSDOM/static-CSS coverage for cockpit state, attention priority, project aliases, multi-open disclosures and responsive layout;
- deliberately defer Observe/Code presets: M6 requires an exact capability-delta preview before a preset may apply anything, and this slice adds no second permission workflow.

## Security contract

No capability defaults, main-process enforcement, IPC, connector registration, filesystem/network authority, sandboxing, read-only semantics or cached-schema enforcement changes. The cockpit mirrors application-owned renderer projections; granular switches and read-only mode remain the only authority-changing controls on Home.

